        "credit": "(Credit: X-ray (NASA/CXC/Durham Univ./D.Alexander et al.); Optical (NASA/ESA/STScI/IoA/S.Chapman et al.); Lyman-alpha Optical (NAOJ/Subaru/Tohoku Univ./T.Hayashino et al.); Infrared (NASA/JPL-Caltech/",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Composite_Image_of_a_Blob_(2009-labs-more-1_-_labs_noxray).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.82,
      "end": 9.04,
      "text": "Astronomers in 2000 discovered hydrogen blobs spanning 400,000 light-years across.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lyman-alpha blob LAB-1.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/M. Hayes",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lyman-alpha_blob_LAB-1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.833,
          "end": 6.767,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 6.767,
          "end": 9.033,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.04,
      "end": 13.2,
      "text": "Using the Subaru Telescope, team members found 30 more along a cosmic filament.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Subaru and Keck Telescopes. Mauna Kea Summit (503960) (22086583112).jpg",
        "credit": "Robert Linsdell from St. Andrews, Canada",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Subaru_and_Keck_Telescopes._Mauna_Kea_Summit_(503960)_(22086583112).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.033,
          "end": 11.133,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 11.133,
          "end": 13.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.2,
      "end": 16.62,
      "text": "Nothing that huge should shine so brightly billions of light-years away.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 16.633,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 16.62,
      "end": 20.4,
      "text": "Scientists debated if gas was falling in or supernovas were blowing out.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "HST SN 1987A 20th anniversary.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, P. Challis, and R. Kirshner (Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HST_SN_1987A_20th_anniversary.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.633,
          "end": 20.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.4,
      "end": 24.48,
      "text": "But polarized light proved the primary power was hidden inside.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ESO Very Large Telescope (kamphues08D31034).jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/F. Kamphues",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ESO_Very_Large_Telescope_(kamphues08D31034).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.4,
          "end": 24.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.48,
      "end": 28.54,
      "text": "Supermassive black holes inside act like cosmic lightbulbs, illuminating the gas.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of supermassive black hole seed.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/CXC/M. Weiss",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_supermassive_black_hole_seed.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.467,
          "end": 28.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.54,
      "end": 32.903,
      "text": "These hidden engines explain how giant gas clouds dwarf our galaxy.",
